proposed.condition:
Let the supremum below range over the gamma-separated laws \(P\in\mathcal P_{\mathrm S}\) and the common deterministic learner schedules satisfying the applicable heavy- and Gaussian-arm hypotheses at sample size \(n\).  The scalar coordinates of the moving row laws satisfy
\[
\lim_{\eta\downarrow0}\limsup_{n\to\infty}
\sup_P\max_{\tau\in\mathcal T}\sup_{x\in\mathbb R}
P\bigl\{|Z_{P,n}(\tau)-x|\le\eta\bigr\}=0.
\]
